# Spec / research sync order

If `docs/test-task.md`, `docs/SPEC.md`, or KB files change:

## Sync order (mandatory)

1. **`docs/research/07d-impl-kb-adr-dod.md`** — update ADR decisions + Must DoD checkboxes  
2. **`docs/research/07c-impl-kb-slices.md`** — adjust slice exit/gates if scope moved  
3. **`docs/research/07a-…` / `07b-…`** — only sections touched by the change  
4. **`docs/research/07-implementation-kb-overview.md`** — traceability rows if IDs changed  
5. **`docs/research/03-decisions.md`** + **`docs/research/README.md`** — one-line pointers if needed  

Do **not** rewrite architecture report (`02-…`) unless the locked stack changes.

## Conflict rule

`test-task.md` (TQ) wins → then SPEC → then ADR → then other KB prose.

## After sync

Note the change in ADR file under a short “Changelog” bullet (date + what flipped).
